MS: That's a picture of my son Simon-- from left to right-- and his wife. In the middle is my granddaughter in her bat mitzvah.

INT: What is her name?

MS: Debbie. And my son Lee, with his wife.

INT: And what is his wife's name?

MS: Barbara.

INT: And when was this taken-- what year?

MS: This was taken in 1983.

INT: Where was it taken? Do you remember?

MS: Here in-- in-- in the valley.

INT: OK?

MS: That's a picture of my brother Hugo. That was taken in 1943, in Sighet. And he's the one who didn't make it. He broke his leg, in-- in the camp, while working. And that's the last anybody has seen him of. I couldn't get any information what happened to him.

INT: OK?

MS: That's a picture of my mother and her sister. My mother is the one on the left-- Blanka-- and her sister [? Frida. ?] That picture was taken in 1920, in Sighet, Hungary.

